all prove later that 𝐼𝑑⁡(𝐷) is always a positive real number for every 𝑑-ary tree 𝐷—see Proposition 8. For the particular case where 𝑑=2, it was conjectured in [6] that the asymptotic formula (2)max|𝑇|=𝑛𝑇binary tree⁡𝛾⁡(𝐵,𝑇)=𝐼2⁡(𝐵)+𝒪⁡(𝑛−1)holds for every binary tree 𝐵. In the present work, we affirm this conjecture, and even generalize the result to every 𝑑≥2 (Theorem 3).\n## 4. Inducibility vs. Maximum density\n\nOur first goal in this section is to prove a conjecture from [6] which states that the maximum of 𝛾⁡(𝐷,𝑇) over 𝑑-ary trees 𝑇 with 𝑛 leaves converges fairly quickly to the inducibility 𝐼𝑑⁡(𝐷), namely at a rate of 𝑛−1. To be precise, the conjecture was only made in the binary case.\n\nConjecture 1\n\n## [6]\n\nFor a binary tree 𝐵, we have max|𝑇|=𝑛𝑇binary tree⁡𝛾⁡(𝐵,𝑇)=𝑖2⁡(𝐵)+𝒪⁡(𝑛−1).\n\nWe prove:\n\nTheorem 3\n\nFor every fixed positive integer 𝑑≥2 and every 𝑑-ary tree 𝐷, we have max|𝑇|=𝑛𝑇𝑑-ary tree⁡𝛾⁡(𝐷,𝑇)=𝐼𝑑⁡(𝐷)+𝒪⁡(𝑛−1)for all 𝑛≥|𝐷|. In particular, lim𝑛→∞⁡max|𝑇|=𝑛𝑇𝑑-ary tree⁡𝛾⁡(𝐷,𝑇)=𝐼𝑑⁡(𝐷).Moreover, the sequence given by max|𝑇|=𝑛𝑇𝑑-ary tree⁡𝛾⁡(𝐷,𝑇)is nonincreasing in 𝑛.\n\nProof of Theorem 3\n\nFix 𝑑≥2. Let 𝐷 and 𝑇 be arbitrary 𝑑-ary trees such that |𝐷|≤|𝑇|. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Equations defining probability tree models (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/323165015_Equations_defining_probability_tree_models?_tp=eyJjb250ZXh0Ijp7InBhZ2UiOiJwdWJsaWNhdGlvbiIsInByZXZpb3VzUGFnZSI6bnVsbCwic3ViUGFnZSI6bnVsbH19)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.7 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; terms of (maximal) path di ﬀ erences and then use these results to understand the ideal of model ... In the discussion at the end of this paper, we conjecture that this is the case because for ... Let T be a staged tree.\nThese generators form a Gr¨obner basis with respect to the reverse lexicographical term order.\n\n7. Discussion\n\nThroughout this text we have analysed the algebraic and geometric pro